  "body": "## What happens\nA PR that changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` gets a quick-gate plan of 127 steps (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run`): the post suites and about 70 app suites. The plan has no step for `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` or `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n\nThe catalog tests post the committed examples with the shipped post scripts and compare the result with the committed `.nc` files (`examples/catalog/**`). A change of a post script can change these programs.\n\n## Proof\nPR #3478 at head f9b38a9d7, trial merge with `main` 835556814:\n- quick gate: 127 steps, 0 failed;\n- `cargo xtask gate test catalog_multiaxis_indexed --crate camcraft-app --binary example_catalog`: 2 failed (`regenerates`, `rebuilds`), because `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc` gets new lines.\n\nA review that uses the quick gate reports \"all touched suites green\" for a PR that makes `main` red. The batch gate after the merge finds it too late.\n\n## Wanted\n- The gate map selects the `example_catalog*` app suites when the diff changes a file in `assets/posts/` (and other inputs of the catalog: `assets/machines/`, `examples/catalog/`).\n- A test in `xtask/` pins the selection.\n- If a catalog suite is too slow for the quick tier, select only the cases that use the changed post.\n\nThe PR has `Process change: yes` (it changes `xtask/`).\n",
